# OPERATOR STATE. `make pi-ship` does not overwrite the copy on the Pi
# (PI_OWNED in the Makefile). git holds only the seed for a fresh
# install. Edit on the Pi: `sudo pf tui`, Agent lists, then apply.
#
# With PARANOID=0, this list only decides which hosts stay out of
# unknown.jsonl. With PARANOID=1, this list and the host column of
# core.hosts are the ONLY set of names that the agent segment may reach
# on 443 (docs/paranoid_mode.md). A name allows itself and all its
# subdomains. Thus do not list a subdomain of a name that is already here.
github.com
raw.githubusercontent.com
objects.githubusercontent.com
release-assets.githubusercontent.com
api.anthropic.com
platform.claude.com
claude.ai
api.openai.com
api.x.ai
http-intake.logs.us5.datadoghq.com
registry.npmjs.org
www.npmjs.com
pypi.org
files.pythonhosted.org
proxy.golang.org
sum.golang.org
cloud.google.com
pf-core-echo.test

# --- build mirrors: read-mostly, no anonymous write sink. Thus the worst
# that an agent can do with one is fetch. Uncomment what a build needs. A
# name that nobody fetches should not be on the list.
#deb.debian.org
#security.debian.org
#archive.ubuntu.com
#security.ubuntu.com
#ports.ubuntu.com
#dl-cdn.alpinelinux.org
#crates.io
#static.crates.io
#index.crates.io
#static.rust-lang.org
#rubygems.org
#repo.maven.apache.org
#repo1.maven.org
#repo.packagist.org
#registry.yarnpkg.com
#nodejs.org
#golang.org
#go.dev
#pkg.go.dev
#dl.google.com
#download.docker.com

# --- container registries. A read is a fetch. A push with a token is an
# upload of all that the agent put in a layer. Consider that as you
# consider github.com below.
#registry-1.docker.io
#auth.docker.io
#index.docker.io
#production.cloudflare.docker.com
#ghcr.io
#quay.io
#mcr.microsoft.com

# --- write sinks. Each of these accepts data as its purpose. Thus each
# one that you add gives a capability and removes a guarantee. That is a
# fair trade when the agent needs it, and a bad trade when it does not.
#
# github.com above is already in this class, but it has no such mark. It
# carries api.github.com and gist.github.com. Thus an agent that has a
# token can publish a secret gist today. That is not a reason to remove
# it. It is the honest price of the list.
#hooks.slack.com
#api.slack.com
#api.telegram.org
#storage.googleapis.com
#s3.amazonaws.com
#sentry.io

# --- considered and rejected. PaaS wildcards (vercel.app, workers.dev,
# herokuapp.com, netlify.app, pages.dev, fly.dev, onrender.com,
# repl.co, glitch.me) are where a throwaway exfil endpoint lives. But
# they also host a large part of the ordinary web. A block on
# blacklist.domains would really break house browsing, and the agent
# does not need them denied twice. The same for URL shorteners: a real
# exfil channel, small bandwidth, high breakage. They are not on either
# list on purpose. Add them when a session really shows the traffic.
